# Independent audit: joint shell information and partial credit

Source: `candidate a4838c03130dd4a9`, Sections1–4.

Result: **PASS**. The full-information objective is correctly identified as coupling-independent; the partial-information table is a valid lower relaxation for the actual specified coupling.

Expanding C_theta gives sum_j theta_j sum_z alpha_z nu_z(H_j) for every coupling of the fixed physical cone marginals. Thus adjoining the exact source-minus-target surplus restores the actual fixed cap loss identically. No choice of a transport coupling can change that full expectation. This is an exact information statement, not an obstruction to choosing a different real cap menu or body variation.

The Boolean minimization defining c_R has an actual feasible completion on every sample. Allowing unrealizable extra completions can only lower its value, so equation(8) is valid. Increasing retained information is pointwise monotone for the same actual joint law. The warning against treating arbitrary feasible signature tables as an attained geometric certificate is necessary and correctly retained.

For the actual tilted five-rectangle menu, the retained source signatures are deterministic(000),(111),(111). I independently checked every nontrivial subset cost:

    empty:35t1+8t2-8t1t2;
    s:35t1+8t2;
    a or{s,a}:35+8t2;
    b or{s,b}:8+35t1;
    {a,b} or{s,a,b}:43.

Using target marginals1/2 and the printed intersections79/160,79/160,1/2 with weights3/10,3/10,2/5 gives exactly1753/100,43/2,39,51/2,43 as stated. The strict payment43 comes from the two genuinely fully captured exclusive source fibers. It is not attributed to transport optimization. The reference geometry supplies all actual compatibility and criticality conditions; its cylindrical-vs-tilted comparison has the correct sign in the normalized response.

The independent rerun of `supporting computation verify_joint_shell_signature_information_defect_transport.py` passes104 exact checks. No correction requested.
